                    insight_won:            `Won the right way: you diagnosed the real gap, designed a deliverable transfer-focused journey, held the 35% margin inside the €1.8M cap, and defended a feasible 16-week launch. Relevance, margin, faculty and speed all held — the bid your CFO signs and Continentale believes.`,
                    insight_marginblown:    `Won badly — the margin is blown. The design is relevant, but you are below the 35% floor (or over the €1.8M cap). You may take the deal, but it dilutes the portfolio and sets a loss-making precedent your CFO will not tolerate — and weakens the wider €3.1M relationship.`,
                    insight_undeliverable:  `Relevant but undeliverable: the diagnosis and margin hold, but you either over-promised scarce faculty or have no credible plan to launch cohort one in 16 weeks. A great design you cannot staff or land on time loses trust by week six.`,
                    insight_lost:           `Lost the bid: the design read as a catalogue best-of, not a diagnosed custom solution, and the consultancy won on relevance. Re-examine whether you designed from the brief's label instead of the underlying gap.`,
                    insight_belowfloor:     `You finished below the 35% contribution-margin floor. Custom programs win on diagnosed relevance, not on discounting — every euro you dropped to undercut the consultancy came straight out of the margin your CFO defends.`,
                    insight_overcap:        `You breached the €1.8M client budget cap. However relevant the design, procurement screens out a bid over the cap before the CHRO hears the diagnosis. Relevance has to be designed to the budget, not above it.`,
                    insight_overpromise:    `You over-promised the star faculty. Only 24 days exist between the two academics the client trusts; a design that needs more either backfills with names the client never approved or leaves the brochure faces out of the room.`,
                    insight_launch:         `Launch readiness is low — there is no credible plan to put cohort one live in 16 weeks. The board sees a live cohort in week sixteen; a phased MVP is how you deliver that without cutting quality.`,
                    insight_balanced:       `You made the four-way trade-off explicit instead of wishing it away — relevance, margin, faculty and speed all defensible. That is the discipline behind sustainable custom programs.`,

                    hint_overcap:           `You are over the €1.8M cap — procurement will screen you out. Cut bespoke cost or scale a component digitally to bring the design back inside the client budget.`,
